śuna","viṣayī durjana    sadā kāma-rata","    kichhu nāhi mora guṇa"],"translation":["O Gopīnāth, hear my prayer. I am a wicked, constantly covetous materialist. I do not have any good qualities."],"isLong":false},{"number":"2","text":["    gopīnāth, āmāra bharasā tumi","tomāra charaṇe    la-inu śaraṇa","    tomāra kiṅkara āmi"],"translation":["O Gopīnāth, You are my hope. I have taken shelter at Your feet. I am Your servant."],"isLong":false},{"number":"3","text":["    gopīnāth, kemane śodhibe more","nā jāni bhakati    karme jaḍa-mati","    paḍechhi saṁsāra ghore"],"translation":["O Gopīnāth, how will You purify me? I do not understand devotion and my materialistic mind is absorbed in karma. I have fallen into this dark world."],"isLong":false},{"number":"4","text":["    gopīnāth, sakali tomāra māyā","nāhi mama bala    jñāna sunirmala","    svādhīna nahe e kāyā"],"translation":["O Gopīnāth, everything is Your illusion. I have no strength or transcendental knowledge, and this body of mine is not independent (of material nature’s control)."],"isLong":false},{"number":"5","text":["    gopīnāth, niyata charaṇe sthāna","māge e pāmara    kā̐diyā kā̐diyā","    karahe karuṇā dāna"],"translation":["O Gopīnāth, weeping and weeping, this sinner begs for an eternal place at Your feet. Please give him Your mercy."],"isLong":false},{"number":"6","text":["    gopīnāth, tumi ta sakali pāra","durjane tārite    tomāra śakati","    ke āchhe pāpīra āra"],"translation":["O Gopīnāth, You can do anything. You have the power to deliver sinners, and who is a greater sinner than myself?"],"isLong":false},{"number":"7","text":["    gopīnāth, tumi kṛpā-pārābāra","jīvera kāraṇe    āsiyā prapañche","    līlā kaile suvistāra"],"translation":["O Gopīnāth, You are an ocean of mercy. You came into this world and performed Your Pastimes for the sake of the fallen souls."],"isLong":false},{"number":"8","text":["    gopīnāth, āmi ki doṣera doṣī","asura sakala    pāila charaṇa","    vinoda thākila vasi"],"translation":["O Gopīnāth, am I the greatest sinner of all? All the demons reached Your feet, and only this Bhakti Vinod remained sitting here."],"isLong":false}],"resources":{"audio":[{"title":"Srila B.S. Govinda Dev-Goswami Maharaj","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/krsnachaitanya-das/37-gopinath-mama-nivedana-suna-4","personSlug":"srila-b-s-govinda-dev-goswami-maharaj"},{"title":"Srila B.R. Madhusudan Maharaj","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bharatimaharaj/madhusudan-maharaj-gopinath-1","personSlug":"srila-b-r-madhusudan-maharaj"},{"title":"Srila B.R. Madhusudan Maharaj","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bharatimaharaj/madhusudan-maharaj-gopinath","personSlug":"srila-b-r-madhusudan-maharaj"},{"title":"Manasa Krishna Prabhu","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/huron/gopinath-mama-nivedana-suno","personSlug":"manasa-krishna-prabhu"}]},"hasWbw":false,"hasVersesText":true,"hasVersesTranslations":true,"hasLongVerses":false,"fullInlineWbw":false},"telegraphUrl":"https://telegra.ph/Nivedana-02-22-3"},"head":{"canonical":"/en-pe/gopinath-mama-nivedana-shiuno/","description":"Nivedana — a Vaiṣṇava song by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur with lyrics, English translation and word-by-word meaning. From Pocket Kirtan Guide.","title":"Nivedana. by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur. Part 1 | Kirtan Site"},"kind":"song","route":{"kind":"item","bookId":"en-pe","slug":"gopinath-mama-nivedana-shiuno"}}